WHY the direction differs -- computed, not asserted.  The gap is a ratio of two
quantities that each fall with capacity, so its direction is set by WHICH falls faster.
   family       phi* x-drop   phiLRU x-drop       gap
   uniform              4.2             2.0     GROWS
   powerlaw1            7.7             5.5     GROWS
   powerlaw2            4.3             7.7   shrinks
   hotset               3.0             4.7   shrinks
   scan8                4.2             2.0     GROWS
   scan64               4.0             1.9     GROWS
   -> the gap grows exactly when the OPTIMUM improves faster than the policy does: the
      mechanism is how much freedom the clairvoyant has, a property of the workload.

